WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.350
A key member of the "family" will be missing
from the latest installment in the Fast and

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.400
Furious franchise.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.080
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson, who has portrayed
Luke Hobbs in the series ever since 2011's

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.280
Fast Five, will be sitting out the action
when the latest entry hits theaters this summer.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.660
Given his rocky history with franchise star
Vin Diesel, and the success of last year's

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.960
spin-off Fast and Furious Presents: Hobbs
&amp; Shaw, fans could be forgiven for thinking

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.040
that Johnson might be going his own way.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.140
However, that doesn't appear to be the case.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:32.140
In a 2019 interview with MTV News, Johnson
explained that his absence from F9 was due

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.460
to scheduling conflicts with Hobbs &amp; Shaw.
an explanation which seemed a little suspect.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.660
At the time, the spin-off flick had just wrapped,
and when asked by the interviewer if he and

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:44.720
co-star Jason Statham would be taking part
in the ninth film in the main series, Johnson

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:45.720
hemmed and hawed.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:46.420
He said:

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:52.540
"The plan has always been for the Fast and
Furious universe to grow and expand.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.300
As of now, we are not in Fast 9 because they're
getting ready to start shooting."

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.980
We suppose that even the Rock needs to take
a breather from action movies every once in

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:00.480
awhile.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.780
Still, considering that his work on Hobbs
&amp; Shaw was complete and F9 was gearing up

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:09.460
to enter production at the time of the interview,
it sure seems like he could have participated.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.420
Perhaps that answer wasn't quite the whole
truth.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:16.020
It's well-documented that Johnson and Diesel
butted heads, and possibly biceps, during

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.670
the making of 2017's Fate of the Furious.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:22.240
While we still don't know the exact nature
of the beef, we do know that it was serious

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.660
enough that the two didn't actually shoot
any scenes for the flick together.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:30.080
Instead, clever editing and Dom's seeming
betrayal of his Family allowed the two bald

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:33.790
beefcakes to share starring roles without
actually sharing a scene.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:38.200
However, in a Rolling Stone interview in 2018,
Johnson indicated that the beef had been at

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.329
least somewhat squashed.

00:01:39.329 --> 00:01:40.640
According to The Rock himself:

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.380
"Right now I'm concentrating on making [Hobbs
&amp; Shaw] as good as it can be.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:48.320
But I wish him all the best, and I harbor
no ill will there, just because of the clarity

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:48.820
we have...

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.580
Actually, you can erase that last part about
'no ill will.'

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.140
We'll just keep it with the clarity."

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:57.560
That's a little harsh, but by September of
last year, the Rock seemed like he was finally

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.440
ready to put all the bad blood behind him.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.560
Johnson made an Instagram post thanking his
former co-star for all his support.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:04.200
Johnson said:

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:07.120
"I want to thank brother Vin for your support
of Hobbs &amp; Shaw.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:11.520
We did it the right way, we did it the smart
way, and again brother, I appreciate your

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.120
support.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.240
And of course, all roads lead to one thing...

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:15.980
I'll be seeing you soon, Toretto."

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:19.980
Johnson's reference to Diesel's character
in the series certainly implies that Hobbs

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.880
will be back to mix it up with him once again
— but if so, he's running out of road.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.560
"Daddy's gotta go to work."

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:35.750
It has been widely reported that Fast and
Furious 10 will officially bring to a close

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:39.580
the series that Universal Pictures is now
referring to as the "Fast Saga."

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.620
Considering that the finish line is in sight,
it doesn't seem like Johnson would let a little

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:47.480
thing like a three-year old beef keep him
from appearing in the final film of the series.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:53.120
"Look, at the end of the day, the truth is,
there's unfinished business between Hobbs

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:53.620
and Dom.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:54.800
It's unfinished."

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:59.360
While nothing has been officially confirmed,
the rumor mill has gone into overdrive reporting

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:03.660
that anonymous inside sources insist that
Johnson will return for Fast 10.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.240
It's also worth mentioning that John Cena,
who will appear in F9 as Toretto's long-lost

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.380
brother, has done a bit of blabbing to the
press about the possibility.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:15.660
Asked about the likelihood of an onscreen
showdown between himself and Johnson, Cena

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.820
all but confirmed that it was happening before
seeming to catch himself.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:19.820
According to Cena:

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:24.660
"I will say this, man, it's amazing the parallels
that Fast runs with WWE.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.880
In Fast, never say never."

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:31.020
Well, we're certainly not going to be the
ones to say "never."

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:34.880
Bringing the Rock back into the mix for the
conclusion of the high-octane Fast Saga is

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:40.100
likely to yield only one result: the fastest,
most furious flick of the whole bunch.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.420
"This time, it ain't just about being fast."

